  "description": "Fighters of Record of Ragnarok for Teamfight Manager 2: Lu Bu, Thor, Zeus, Adam, Poseidon, Sasaki Kojiro, Heracles, Jack the Ripper, Raiden Tameemon, Shiva, Buddha, Zerofuku, Hades, Qin Shi Huang, Beelzebub, Nikola Tesla, Leonidas, Apollo, Okita Soji, Susanoo, Simo Häyhä, Loki. Kits are our own designs after the manga's fights: Lu Bu's Shield Breaker counts his blows double against shields and shatters them for real (the pack's own code, ragnarok.dll); Thor brings down Thor's Hammer and his Mjolnir flies out and back to his hand, awakening on every third skill; Zeus fires the Meteor Jab, swells into his muscle body once he warms up and presses it down into Adamas for his ultimate; Adam reads every move with God Reader, dodges it and hits back with a copy, down to the Fist That Transcends Time; Poseidon needs no one - alone he hits harder and takes less (the pack's own code), thrusts with Amphitrite, rains down Chione Tyro Demeter and floods a target for forty days and nights; Sasaki Kojiro, the greatest loser in history, learns every foe he strikes and hits them harder each time (the pack's own code), turns his blade back with Swallow Return, reads every move with Manju Muso and cuts Soen Zanko Manjin Ryoran with the two swords of Niten Ganryu; Heracles, the god of justice who fights for humanity, spreads the brand of his Twelve Labors with every skill (the pack's own code) and makes his pact with Cerberus for his ultimate, ending it with the Great Hero's Fist; Jack the Ripper sees the colour of every heart and strikes the frightened harder (the pack's own code), parries with an umbrella his gloves made divine and throws a knife that Dear God made a divine weapon; Raiden Tameemon, the strongest sumo wrestler, breaks his Hundred Seals to unbind the muscles he held back all his life before his first Yatagarasu, which closes in at once, slaps with Tsuppari and stamps the ground; Shiva dances the Tandava with four arms (the pack's own code), kicks down in flames with Krittivasa and pumps his heart alight for Tandava Karma, ending it with Deva Loka; Buddha, the god who turned his back on the gods, sees every blow coming with Future Sight, turns his Six Realms Staff into the Twelve Devas Axe and the Shield of Ahimsa and cuts with the Great Nirvana Sword Zero; Zerofuku, the god of misfortune, marks his foes with misfortune and swings a Misery Cleaver that grows on it, until Hajun devours him from within and breaks out of a dark cocoon for the rest of his life, with arm blades, the Heaven-Piercing Demon Drill and Arataka; Hades, king of the underworld and eldest of the three brothers, strikes with Persephone Kallichore and Persephone Titan and forges the Ichor Desmos with his own blood for Ichor Eos; Qin Shi Huang, the first emperor, sees the stars in his foes and weakens them with a breath of Drifting Tortoise, catches their force with the Chiyou Armor Sleeves and turns it back, shielding his allies, and stores it in the Goujian sword for his Swallow Cut (the pack's own code); Beelzebub, lord of the flies, makes everything his skills touch vibrate and lose its magic resist, sends waves from his bone staff, raises the Gates of Hell and crushes his foes into the black core of the False God Chaos, which tears into him too; Nikola Tesla fights in his Super Automaton Beta, his plasma fists hitting twice, drops the Prison of the Gods on his foes and, while it stands, warps onto them, and ends with the Plasma Pulse Punch Cross; Leonidas, king of Sparta, guards the allies around him like a phalanx, hurls his shield on its chain with Phalanx Enchos, raises it to send back what hits him and charges with Phalanx Lambda behind the Shield of Truth; Apollo, god of the sun, grows brighter the more champions are near (the pack's own code), binds his foes with Artemis Elenchos, looses the Moonlight of Artemis and has her statue shoot him at them as Argyrotoxos, the soul-piercing silver arrow; Okita Soji packs a life's swordsmanship into one moment, thrusts three times at godspeed, turns Demon Child and lunges with Tensho Sandanzuki; Susanoo answers every blade from his seigan stance, cuts the air into the crescent of Ama no Magaeshi and, empty-handed, swings the unseen Musoken that cuts only bones and wears down his own life; Simo Häyhä pays with his own organs for god-killing rounds, fires Ilmatar, Lemminkäinen and Mielikki in turn, vanishes into the snow and ends it with Ukonvasara; Loki's full-power double copies his chained hook, he leaves a copy in black mist and swaps places with another, and Heimskringla raises an army of copied gods' weapons. Sharper frames from ragnarok.dll itself, with or without the League of Legends Heroes and Teamfight Tactics Heroes packs. Chibi (Q-version) pixel art for every hero, effects, icons and sound effects made for this pack; Japanese voice lines from the official promotional recordings (Okita's and Simo's are synthesized: neither has an official recording yet). Non-commercial fan project; Record of Ragnarok (c) its creators and publishers.",
